6"] ["answer-e60983fa-e6a9-5ac0-89a9-689d559fbabd" :answer/id #uuid "e60983fa-e6a9-5ac0-89a9-689d559fbabd"] ["answer-e60983fa-e6a9-5ac0-89a9-689d559fbabd" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e60983fa-e6a9-5ac0-89a9-689d559fbabd" :answer/value "s>{s}_{0}-6"] ["answer-field-3e04132d-f893-5504-93e7-bc8007db050d" :answer-field/key "field-4"] ["answer-field-3e04132d-f893-5504-93e7-bc8007db050d" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select] ["answer-field-3e04132d-f893-5504-93e7-bc8007db050d" :answer-field/correct "answer-e60983fa-e6a9-5ac0-89a9-689d559fbabd"] ["answer-field-3e04132d-f893-5504-93e7-bc8007db050d" :answer-field/choices "answer-bc516240-edf6-50de-a972-2d32bd44c276"] ["answer-field-3e04132d-f893-5504-93e7-bc8007db050d" :answer-field/choices "answer-e9fce1b0-8710-5564-a541-83b6838d2cc1"] ["answer-field-3e04132d-f893-5504-93e7-bc8007db050d" :answer-field/choices "answer-e60983fa-e6a9-5ac0-89a9-689d559fbabd"] ["question-bf25d1c4-52d6-5c8a-89b9-2f0b3253eb28" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-74110f7b-0273-51e4-a4d8-5ebb7a3df510"] ["question-bf25d1c4-52d6-5c8a-89b9-2f0b3253eb28" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-5331794b-edb9-5987-ad14-749201d4047c"] ["question-bf25d1c4-52d6-5c8a-89b9-2f0b3253eb28" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-0be05dc0-5dcb-5229-97d5-3889f2b77acc"] ["question-bf25d1c4-52d6-5c8a-89b9-2f0b3253eb28" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-3e04132d-f893-5504-93e7-bc8007db050d"] [17592186221436 :knowledge-point/questions "question-bf25d1c4-52d6-5c8a-89b9-2f0b3253eb28"] [17592186368088 :question/problem "Given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{t}^{n}\\} & =\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}, &  & s>0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nuse linearity of Laplace transforms and the first shifting theorem to find the Laplace transform of $f(t)=7{t}^{2}+5{t}^{4}{e}^{t}$ for $s>1.$"] [17592186368088 :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the linearity properties of Laplace transforms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{f(t)\\} & =L\\{7{t}^{2}+5{t}^{4}{e}^{t}\\} \\\\  & =L\\{7{t}^{2}\\}+L\\{5{t}^{4}{e}^{t}\\} \\\\  & =7L\\{{t}^{2}\\}+5L\\{{t}^{4}{e}^{t}\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are given that, for $s>0,$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{t}^{n}\\} & =\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{t}^{2}\\} & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}} \\\\ L\\{{t}^{4}\\} & =\\frac{24}{{s}^{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first shifting theorem states that if $L\\{f(t)\\}=F(s),$ then $L\\{{e}^{at}f(t)\\}=F(s-a).$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nL\\{{t}^{4}{e}^{t}\\}=\\frac{24}{(s-1)^{5}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{f(t)\\} & =7L\\{{t}^{2}\\}+5L\\{{t}^{4}{e}^{t}\\} \\\\  & =7\\cdot \\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+5\\cdot \\frac{24}{(s-1)^{5}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{120}{(s-1)^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis transform is valid for $s>1.$"] ["activity-c46cfffe-18b2-5eac-8e1f-91eedc4c8269" :activity/id #uuid "c46cfffe-18b2-5eac-8e1f-91eedc4c8269"] ["step-f579c56e-583e-5d0a-8431-cb59e1d5eecc" :step/id #uuid "f579c56e-583e-5d0a-8431-cb59e1d5eecc"] ["step-4352ef4f-23b6-5c61-ac25-56e4098a43c6" :step/id #uuid "4352ef4f-23b6-5c61-ac25-56e4098a43c6"] ["step-34e3daa2-8ba3-59ec-8c00-c52a7eef4a03" :step/id #uuid "34e3daa2-8ba3-59ec-8c00-c52a7eef4a03"] ["step-f579c56e-583e-5d0a-8431-cb59e1d5eecc" :step/content "question-002b6494-db6e-5c52-baa6-f8349498d2c1"] ["step-f579c56e-583e-5d0a-8431-cb59e1d5eecc" :step/next "step-4352ef4f-23b6-5c61-ac25-56e4098a43c6"] ["step-4352ef4f-23b6-5c61-ac25-56e4098a43c6" :step/content "question-bf25d1c4-52d6-5c8a-89b9-2f0b3253eb28"] ["step-4352ef4f-23b6-5c61-ac25-56e4098a43c6" :step/next "step-34e3daa2-8ba3-59ec-8c00-c52a7eef4a03"] ["step-34e3daa2-8ba3-59ec-8c00-c52a7eef4a03" :step/content 17592186368088] ["activity-c46cfffe-18b2-5eac-8e1f-91eedc4c8269" :activity/title "The First Shifting Theorem of Laplace Transforms"] ["activity-c46cfffe-18b2-5eac-8e1f-91eedc4c8269" :activity/type :activity.type/review] ["activity-c46cfffe-18b2-5eac-8e1f-91eedc4c8269